vyatta-kernel-forwarding (0.4) trixie; urgency=medium

  * dp-name: print only names the dataplane-ifname YANG accepts; np, v and
    u (USB) names keep their kernel name

 -- NuDanOS Maintainers <jon@fernandez.tech>  Sat, 03 Oct 2026 19:56:41 -0700

vyatta-kernel-forwarding (0.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Depend on iptables, and select a legacy back end only once its
    alternatives are registered: in the ISO build the postinst ran while
    iptables was unpacked but not configured, and failed.

 -- NuDanOS Maintainers <jon@fernandez.tech>  Fri, 02 Oct 2026 10:02:31 -0700

vyatta-kernel-forwarding (0.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Name NICs with DANOS dataplane names (enp0s3 -> dp0s3) through a udev
    rule and dp-name, and map the dp prefix to the dataplane interface type
    in /opt/vyatta/etc/netdevice.d.
  * New binary vyatta-kernel-forwarding-deviations-v1-yang: refuse the
    DPDK-only cpu-affinity, receive-cpu-affinity and transmit-cpu-affinity
    settings at commit with a message naming the cause.
  * postinst selects the legacy iptables/ip6tables/ebtables back ends
    (DANOS build-iso hook 14-iptables-legacy) and writes the marker file
    /opt/vyatta/etc/kernel-forwarding; postrm removes it.

 -- NuDanOS Maintainers <jon@fernandez.tech>  Fri, 02 Oct 2026 08:24:16 -0700

vyatta-kernel-forwarding (0.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: provides vyatta-forwarding for systems that forward in
    the Linux kernel, so configuration packages no longer require the DPDK
    dataplane.

